				\begin{document}$$\:{Q}_{e\:(mg/g)}=\frac{{(C}_{o}-{C}_{e})V}{m}$$\end{document}

To gain deeper insights into the underlying adsorption mechanism, the experimental data for Ca2+ and Mg2+ uptake were further analyzed using various kinetic and equilibrium models, including advanced isotherm approaches informed by statistical physics (as detailed in Table S1). Nonlinear regression analysis was employed to fit the models to the empirical data. The goodness of fit for each model was evaluated using multiple statistical performance indicators. These included the coefficient of determination (R2) (Eq. 2), Chi-square error (χ2) (Eq. 3), and the root mean square error (RMSE) (Eq. 4), calculated as follows:2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
