The column’s performance was characterized by analyzing key dynamic parameters, including the breakthrough time, saturation time, removal percentage, and the shape of the breakthrough curves. Breakthrough and saturation points were defined as the times corresponding to 10% and 95% breakthrough, respectively. Additional system parameters such as the total volume of treated water (Veff) (Eq. 5), concentration of adsorbed ions (Cad) (Eq. 6), total quantity of ions adsorbed (Qtotal) (Eq. 7), total input ion mass (Mtotal) (Eq. 8), equilibrium adsorption capacity (Qeq) (Eq. 9), and overall ion removal percentage (R%) (Eq. 10) were calculated using the following set of equations:5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
